# Process-compose + Docker

**Skill:** skill `process-compose-docker` (MUST Read and follow when this rule loads).

## MUST

- Name stack up/down `go tool task serve` / `serve-down` or `make serve` / `make serve-down` (not only `dev` / `dev-down`)
- Timed Docker daemon probe before optional container namespaces start
- Ask before continuing without those containers when the probe fails on a TTY
- Stop stacks without `-v` / `--volumes` / `docker volume rm` on the default down path
- Keep durable sidecar state on named volumes
- When the repo has `process-compose.yaml` or `scripts/pc-up.sh` plus `serve` / `serve-down`: prebuild Go services to a named binary before `process-compose up`, exec that binary to listen, set `readiness_probe` on HTTP processes (see skill `process-compose-docker`)

## MUST NOT

- Bare unbounded `docker info` in up scripts
- Silent skip of Docker namespaces on an interactive TTY
- Wipe volumes as part of normal `serve-down` / `process-compose down` / `docker compose down`
- Use `go run` or `wgo run` as the first listen process for Go services in process-compose (readiness must not wait on `go tool link`)
